Package: chordsplay
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11), python3-flask, python3-waitress, python3-mutagen, python3-qrcode
Description: Play your music in the browser with lyrics and guitar chords
 ChordsPlay is a web server for your music collection: any browser plays the
 songs while the page shows each song's lyrics and guitar chords, fetched from
 Ultimate Guitar and drawn as large as the screen allows. One server holds the
 songs, chords, tags, filters and play history.
 .
 The package installs the server as the system service chordsplay.service with
 its own user. Settings are in /etc/chordsplay/chordsplay.env, the data is in
 /var/lib/chordsplay. Publish it through a reverse proxy with a login.

Package: chordsplay-mmp
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11), maneline, python3-numpy, pulseaudio-utils, pipewire-bin, opus-tools
Description: ChordsPlay amp control for the Fender Mustang Micro Plus
 The optional Mustang Micro Plus parts of ChordsPlay, for the computer the amp
 is paired with: the amp bridge, which follows the ChordsPlay page and switches
 the amp to the preset stored for the playing song, and the script that
 measures all presets so they are equally loud (chordsplay-match-levels).
 .
 Both run as systemd user units: chordsplay-amp-bridge.service, which starts
 chordsplay-amp-agent.service (mmp-web from the package maneline).
